menu "Sensor Platform audio analysis"

    config SP_MIC_PCM_RETAIN
        bool "Retain analysis PCM windows (SPIRAM double-buffer)"
        default n
        help
            Keep completed analysis windows as double-buffered SPIRAM PCM for
            every live microphone channel (1..SP_MIC_COUNT_MAX from NVS
            mic_count). Independent of product Observation policy.
            Products that need L0/L1/L2 typically select this with SP_AUDIO_L0.

    config SP_AUDIO_L0
        bool "L0 acoustic measurements (band energy / RMS / crest)"
        default n
        help
            Compile Platform L0 DSP (sp_acoustic_l0). Host-testable combined-scene
            measurements. Does not include product Observation or AE policy.

    config SP_AUDIO_L1
        bool "L1 spectral features (FFT centroid / bandwidth / flatness)"
        default n
        depends on SP_AUDIO_L0
        help
            Compile Platform L1 DSP (sp_acoustic_l1). Requires L0. Uses a static
            FFT workspace (~22.5 KiB).

    config SP_AUDIO_L2
        bool "L2 acoustic dynamics (flux / envelope / dominant delta)"
        default n
        depends on SP_AUDIO_L1
        help
            Compile Platform L2 DSP (sp_acoustic_l2) and enable the fused L1+L2
            FFT path. Requires L1. Invalid without L1 (Kconfig dependency).

endmenu
